# Environments
evenv/
.venv/

# Database and Cache
*.db3
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Logs
**/logs/*
!**/logs/README.md

# Test runner cache. The project runs `evennia test`, not pytest --
# see blackout/README.md "Tests".
.pytest_cache/

# Dead map-parser cache artifacts; regenerable, nothing reads them.
blackout/server/.cache/

# Manual editor backups. Git is the backup; ten of these were committed
# before being cleaned out in the 08/01 audit.
*.sav
*.sav[0-9]

# notes
*.todo
*.todo.md
*.note
*.note.md

# Local/backup variants of operator scripts
blackout/scripts/*.local
blackout/scripts/*.dan
# Planning and design docs are working documents, not deliverables.
#
# The flow is: write one, implement it, move it to docs/old/. It never gets
# committed -- the CODE is what carries the decision, and CLAUDE.md is where a
# rule that outlives the doc goes. A committed plan is one that has to be kept
# in step with a tree that has already moved past it.
#
# Ignoring the whole directory does NOT untrack the handful of older docs that
# were already committed before this rule; git ignores .gitignore for files it
# already tracks. It only stops new ones being added by a wide `git add`.
docs/
